summary.novel_idea:
The authors derive modified Boltzmann hierarchy equations (BHEs) that explicitly account for non-zero zeroth-order collision terms ($C_{
u}^{(0)} 
eq 0$) in cosmological neutrino self-interactions. They show that low-energy renormalizable extensions leading to $
u$SI intrinsically feature resonant mediator behavior ($T_
u \sim M$), invalidating standard relativistic fluid assumptions and BBN bounds derived from unsuppressed $2\leftrightarrow 1$ thermalization.
